# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env.
#
# There is no mock-data mode any more. EXPO_PUBLIC_USE_SUPABASE used to switch
# it, and this file used to tell you to leave it at 0 — but `USE_SUPABASE` is a
# hardcoded `true` in src/lib/config.ts, nothing reads the variable, and
# following the old instruction got you a `supabaseUrl is required` crash on
# launch. The two Supabase values below are required, not optional.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key
EXPO_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_live_or_test_xxx
# Server-side only (edge functions) — do NOT prefix with EXPO_PUBLIC:
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_or_test_xxx

# ── Posting a card straight to Instagram (optional) ─────────────────────────
#
# Without these the Share Kit still works: it composes the card and hands it to
# the phone's share sheet, which posts to the same account in two taps. What
# they add is the one-tap path, and both halves come from ONE Meta app:
#
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_INSTAGRAM_CLIENT_ID   the Meta app id. Public by design — it is
#                                     in the consent URL every coach sees.
#   INSTAGRAM_CLIENT_ID               the same value, as a SUPABASE SECRET, for
#                                     supabase/functions/instagram-publish.
#   INSTAGRAM_CLIENT_SECRET           the Meta app secret. A Supabase secret and
#                                     nothing else. It is never in the bundle.
#
# The Meta app also needs https://www.repplefitness.com/ads/callback listed
# under Valid OAuth Redirect URIs (the same page the ad-account sign-in uses),
# and instagram_content_publish approved through Meta App Review. Until that
# approval lands the screen says "not available" in those words.
EXPO_PUBLIC_INSTAGRAM_CLIENT_ID=

# ── Which company answers the AI features (server side only) ───────────────
#
# Three edge functions call a model: coach-chat, nutrition-parse and
# vision-analyze. src/lib/llmGateway.ts picks the provider, and the rule is one
# line: CHEAPER_INFERENCE_API_KEY wins if it is set, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is used
# otherwise, and with neither set the three functions refuse.
#
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY          from console.anthropic.com. The default, and what
#                              web/privacy.html describes as the live route.
#   CHEAPER_INFERENCE_API_KEY  the gateway. SETTING THIS SWITCHES EVERY AI
#                              FEATURE OVER, including the ones that send a
#                              member's meal photo, physique photo and InBody
#                              sheet. Before setting it, read the second half of
#                              the AI section of web/privacy.html: that route is
#                              a reseller, its replies are served by further
#                              companies again, and its catalogue offers zero
#                              data retention on none of its models. Unsetting
#                              it is the whole of the rollback — no deploy.
#
# The member-facing consent copy still names Anthropic and only Anthropic
# (src/lib/photoAI.ts, src/lib/scanSheetConsent.ts, src/lib/coachShare.ts). That
# copy is what a member reads before a photograph leaves their phone, so it has
# to be rewritten before the gateway is switched on, not after.
#
# Model overrides, both optional and both naming a model that provider offers.
# They are separate secrets because the names are not interchangeable: the
# Anthropic vision default, claude-3-5-sonnet-latest, is not in the gateway's
# catalogue at all, and the model both providers use for text, claude-sonnet-5,
# is marked as having no vision there.
#
#   ANTHROPIC_MODEL            overrides the Anthropic default.
#   CHEAPER_INFERENCE_MODEL    overrides the gateway default.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
CHEAPER_INFERENCE_API_KEY=
